  "description": "YODYOJ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C99 H82 Fe9 Gd3 O19 1-,2(C16 H36 N1 1+),Cl1 1-. From the CIF bond table, Fe1 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe3 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe4 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe5 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe6 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe7 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe8 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe9 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Fe5C (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe21 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe22 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe23 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe24 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe26 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe27 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe28 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe29 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Fe5' (Fe) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 21 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.815-3.902 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 101.33-109.47°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C131H154ClFe9Gd3N2O19. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
